{"kind": "mod", "id": 2679, "name": "LootNET", "slug": "lootnet", "teaser": "a mod adding a summary of the total loot value of the raid", "owner_name": "20fpsguy", "downloads": 17561, "favourites": 65, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": true, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "com.20fpsguy.lootnet", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Other", "category_id": 17, "updated_at": "2026-08-05T18:36:04.000000Z", "created_at": "2026-05-04T21:14:19.000000Z", "published_at": "2026-05-04T21:17:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.1", "latest_version": "1.1.0", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<h3>UI label style inspired by ShowLootValueInRaid by HiddenCirno</h3>\n<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Features</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><h3>Loot value while you play</h3>\n<p>There’s a counter in your inventory screen that adds up the flea value of everything you’re carrying. It updates as you pick things up. If an item isn’t on the flea, it uses the handbook price instead.</p>\n<h3>Summary when you extract</h3>\n<p>When you make it out, you get a full screen breakdown of the raid: total value, your 5 best finds, how many items you grabbed, your kills, and the XP you earned. It closes on its own after a few seconds, or you can click to skip it. You can change that in the F12 menu.</p>\n<h3>Raid history</h3>\n<p>There’s a HISTORY button added to the main menu. It opens a panel with a card for each raid you’ve done this session, showing the map, whether it was a PMC or Scav run, the loot value, and your kills. It keeps the last 15.</p>\n<h3>PMC and Scav runs</h3>\n<p>On PMC raids it only counts the stuff you found, not your starting gear. On Scav raids it includes your spawn loadout,</p>\n<h3>Pricing</h3>\n<p>Prices are pulled from flea market, so they match what you’d actually see. If something isn’t listed there, it falls back to the handbook price. By default it counts everything, but there’s an option to only include items that cant really be sold on the flea, so the total reflects what you’d actually make rather than what stuff is theoretically worth.</p>\n<h3>PIT Fireteam</h3>\n<p>If you have PIT Fireteam installed, LootNet picks up on it automatically. Your teammates show up in the summary with their kill counts, and squad kills are included in the history panel.</p>\n<h3>Preview</h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/uM87vUZ.jpeg\" alt=\"LootNet Preview\" /></p></div></div></div>\n<h1>Fika preview</h1>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://imgur.com/0ABBZKJ.png\" alt=\"LootNet Preview\" /></p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.0", "spt_version_constraint": "4.0", "content_length": 903352, "downloads": 472, "published_at": "2026-05-04T21:16:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2679/lootnet/1.0.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.0.1", "spt_version_constraint": "4.0", "content_length": 911991, "downloads": 336, "published_at": "2026-05-05T19:02:42.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2679/lootnet/1.0.1", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.0.2", "spt_version_constraint": "4.0", "content_length": 913169, "downloads": 397, "published_at": "2026-05-06T12:12:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2679/lootnet/1.0.2", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.0.3", "spt_version_constraint": "4.0", "content_length": 912469, "downloads": 393, "published_at": "2026-05-07T15:22:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "http